This research delves into resolving problem (PD): \begin{align*}
&\text{Find}~(x,y)\in W_1^1(\mathbb{R},\mathbb{R}^p),~(A,b)~\text{in}~
\mathcal{P}^1(\mathbb{R},\mathrm{Sym}(p))\times\mathbb{R}^p~\text{such that}~\dot{x}
=\mathrm{b}(t,x,y),\\ &\text{with}~\mathrm{b}~\text{Lipschitz relatively to its second argument},~\text{and}~\text{such that}~y~\text{lies in the Bouligand tangent cone at every point of the trajectory of}~x.
\end{align*} General conditions are imposed on this tangent cone, enabling the derivation of necessary and sufficient conditions for solving (PD), expressed as an evolution variational inequality with a nonsmooth, possibly set-valued operator. Several examples illustrate that the developed method can address a variety of optimization and control problems.
